statement.p:
Solve the following system using augmented matrix methods:
\begin{array}{c}
2 x  - 4 y = 18
\\
3 x  - 5 y = 23
\end{array}

solution.p:
SOLUTION: 
We consider x_1 \mbox{Fe}_{2} +x_2 \mbox{O}_{8} \longrightarrow x_3 \mbox{Fe}_{7}\mbox{O}_{9}, which implies \begin{array}{rcrcrcr}2 x_1 \amp  \amp   \amp  - \amp  7 x_{3} \amp  = \amp  0 \\ \amp   \amp  8 x_{2} \amp  - \amp  9 x_{3} \amp  = \amp  0\end{array}
From the augmented matrix \left[\begin{array}{rrrr} 2 \amp   0 \amp   -7 \amp   0 \\ 0 \amp   8 \amp   -9 \amp   0\end{array}\right] we set x_3 = s_1 as a free variable, and thus x_2 = \frac{9}{8} s_1 and x_1 = \frac{7}{2} s_1. We set s_1 = 8 to obtain x_1 = 28, x_2 = 9, and x_3 = 8, and the balanced equation

SOLUTION: 
We consider x_1 \mbox{Na} + x_2 \mbox{H}_{4} \mbox{O} \longrightarrow x_3 \mbox{Na} \mbox{O}_3 \mbox{H}_5 + x_4 \mbox{H}_3, which implies
\begin{array}{rcrcrcrcr} x_1  \amp  \amp   \amp  - \amp  x_{3} \amp  \amp   \amp  = \amp  0 \\ \amp   \amp  4 x_{2} \amp  - \amp  5 x_{3} \amp  - \amp  3 x_{4} \amp  = \amp  0 \\ \amp   \amp  x_{2} \amp  - \amp  3 x_{3} \amp  \amp   \amp  = \amp  0\end{array}
Row-reduce the augmented matrix
\begin{array}{ccc}
\left[\begin{array}{rrrrr} 1 \amp   0 \amp   -1 \amp   0 \amp   0 \\ 0 \amp   4 \amp   -5 \amp   -3 \amp   0 \\ 0 \amp   1 \amp   -3 \amp   0 \amp   0\end{array}\right] \amp  \overset{R_2 \Leftrightarrow R_3}{\sim} \amp  \left[\begin{array}{rrrrr} 1 \amp   0 \amp   -1 \amp   0 \amp   0 \\ 0 \amp   1 \amp   -3 \amp   0 \amp   0 \\ 0 \amp   4 \amp   -5 \amp   -3 \amp   0\end{array}\right] \\ 
 \amp  \overset{-4 R_2 + R_3 \Leftrightarrow R_3}{\sim} \amp  \left[\begin{array}{rrrrr} 1 \amp   0 \amp   -1 \amp   0 \amp   0 \\ 0 \amp   1 \amp   -3 \amp   0 \amp   0 \\ 0 \amp   0 \amp   7 \amp   -3 \amp   0\end{array}\right]
\end{array}
We set x_4 = s_1 as a free variable, and thus x_3 = {\frac{3}{7}} s_1, x_2 = 3 x_3={\frac{9}{7}} s_1, and x_1 = x_3={\frac{3}{7}} s_1. Setting s_1 = 7 gives that x_1 = 3, x_2 = 9, and x_3 = 3, and hence the balanced equation is
3 \mbox{Na}+ 9 \mbox{H}_{4} \mbox{O} \longrightarrow 3 \mbox{Na} \mbox{O}_3 \mbox{H}_5+ 7 \mbox{H}_3.

row.cell:
Find the vector \overrightarrow{AB}
in \mathbb{R}^2 given in the figure.
\overrightarrow{AB} =

Several unit vectors \vec{r}, \vec{s}, \vec{t}, \vec{u}, \vec{n},
and \vec{e} in the xy-plane (not three-dimensional space) are shown in the figure.
Using the geometric definition of the dot product, are the following dot products positive, negative, or zero? 
You may assume that angles that look the same are the same.



\vec{t} \cdot \vec{u}



\vec{r} \cdot \vec{u}



\vec{e} \cdot \vec{s}



\vec{n} \cdot \vec{e}



\vec{e} \cdot \vec{r}



\vec{s} \cdot \vec{t}



\vec{n} \cdot \vec{t}



\vec{r} \cdot \vec{s}

statement.p:
Express the vector \vec{v}= \left[\begin{array}{c}
15\cr
12
\end{array}\right] as a linear combination of \vec{x}= \left[\begin{array}{c}
-2\cr
-5
\end{array}\right] and \vec{y}=\left[\begin{array}{c}
-3\cr
1
\end{array}\right].

Find the determinant of the following 2 \times 2 matrix.
\begin{bmatrix}
\displaystyle  \frac{1}{2} \amp  \displaystyle \frac{1}{5}\thinspace \\
\displaystyle  -\frac{1}{4} \amp  \displaystyle \frac{5}{6}\thinspace 
\end{bmatrix}
